Hi (Joe :),<div><br></div><div>I wish to provide editing feature on a dataset located on server side.</div><div><br></div><div>So here, it works well (without server-side editing) :</div><div>========= ui.R =========</div><div>library(shiny)<br></div><div><div>shinyUI(pageWithSidebar(  </div><div>  headerPanel(&quot;Title2&quot;),</div><div>  sidebarPanel(),</div><div>  mainPanel(</div><div>    h2(&quot;edit&quot;),</div><div>    tags$textarea(id=&quot;texteditor&quot;,&quot;functionnnn foo(items) {
    var x = \&quot;All this is syntax highlighted\&quot;;
    return x;
}&quot;),</div><div>    tags$div(id=&quot;aceeditor&quot;),</div><div>    HTML(readLines(&quot;www/autoselect.js&quot;),</div><div>    h2(&quot;result&quot;),</div><div>    textOutput(&quot;debug&quot;)</div><div>  )</div><div>))</div></div><div><div>==========================</div><div><div><div><div>========= server.R ==========</div><div></div></div><div></div></div></div><div></div></div><div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output) {</div><div>  output$debug &lt;- reactiveText(function() {</div><div>    input$texteditor</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div></div><div><div><div>==========================</div></div></div><div>======= autoselect.js =========<br></div><div><div>&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot; media=&quot;screen&quot;&gt;</div><div>    #aceeditor { </div><div>    height: 275px;</div><div>    position: relative;</div><div>    border: 1px solid #DDD;</div><div>    border-radius: 4px;</div><div>    border-bottom-right-radius: 0px;</div><div>    margin-top: 5px;</div><div>    }</div><div>&lt;/style&gt;</div><div>&lt;script src=&quot;<a href="http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409952909000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0RW_R8MF28I_u88bAPLKxA">http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js</a>&quot; type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</div><div>&lt;script&gt;</div><div>    var aceeditor = ace.edit(&quot;aceeditor&quot;);</div><div>    aceeditor.setTheme(&quot;ace/theme/twilight&quot;);</div><div>    aceeditor.getSession().setMode(&quot;ace/mode/javascript&quot;);</div><div>    </div><div>    var texteditor = $(&#39;textarea[id=&quot;texteditor&quot;]&#39;).hide();</div><div>aceeditor.getSession().setValue(texteditor.val());</div><div><br></div><div>aceeditor.getSession().on(&#39;change&#39;, function(e){</div><div>  texteditor.val(aceeditor.getSession().getValue());</div><div>  texteditor.change();</div><div>});</div><div>    texteditor.onchange = function() {</div><div>        texteditor.select();</div><div>    };</div><div>&lt;/script&gt;</div></div><div><div><div>==========================</div><div></div></div><div></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Now, if I wish to provide server-side editing using uiOutput (in place of tags$textarea) :</div><div>========= ui.R =========<br></div><div><div>library(shiny)</div><div>shinyUI(pageWithSidebar(  </div><div>  headerPanel(&quot;Title2&quot;),</div><div>  sidebarPanel(),</div><div>  mainPanel(</div><div>    h2(&quot;edit&quot;),</div><div>    uiOutput(&quot;textarea&quot;),</div><div>    tags$div(id=&quot;aceeditor&quot;),</div><div>    HTML(readLines(&quot;www/autoselect.js&quot;),</div><div>    h2(&quot;result&quot;),</div><div>    textOutput(&quot;debug&quot;)</div><div>  )</div><div>)))</div></div><div><div>==========================</div><div></div></div><div>========= server.R ==========<br></div><div><div></div></div><div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output) {</div><div>  output$debug &lt;- reactiveText(function() {</div><div>    input$texteditor</div><div>  })</div><div>  output$textarea &lt;- reactiveUI(function() { </div><div>    return(</div><div>      tags$textarea(id=&quot;texteditor&quot;,(paste(readLines(file.path(&quot;test.R&quot;)),collapse=&quot;
&quot;)))</div><div>    )</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div></div><div><div><div>==========================</div><div></div></div><div></div></div><div><br></div><div>it seems that the textarea element is not found by jquery selector in autoselect.js (line &quot;var texteditor = $(&#39;textarea[id=&quot;texteditor&quot;]&#39;).hide();&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>Any idea ?</div>

Thank you Joe for this suggestion, but it did not fix the issue.<div>In fact, it seems that the uiOutput(&quot;textarea&quot;) is not evaluated at the startup of the page, so the jquery $(&#39;textarea[id=&quot;texteditor&quot;]&#39;).hide(); is not applied (as well as replacing by textarea#texteditor).</div><div><br></div><div>I tried to use a jquery plugin name livequery, so the hide() will be applied as soon as the &lt;div id=&quot;textarea&quot;&gt;&lt;textarea&gt;...&lt;/div&gt; appears, but without success. It seems that the jquery plugin is not loaded.</div><div>As I am a beginner in jquery, I suspect it is not related to shiny :)</div><div><br></div><div>Anyway, I finally turnaround the issue with the following change in autoselect.js (whcih should be renamed by the way) :</div><div>======= autoselect.js =========<br></div><div><span style="border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Droid Sans Mono&#39;;white-space:pre;border-spacing:0px"> &lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot; media=&quot;screen&quot;&gt;
    #aceeditor { 
    height: 300px;
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid #DDD;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 0px;
    margin-top: 5px;
    }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;script src=&quot;<a href="http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409952912000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23feibknaYs53R6wHyaTmz">http://d1n0x3qji82z53.cloudfront.net/src-min-noconflict/ace.js</a>&quot; type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script&gt; 
  var aceeditor = ace.edit(&quot;aceeditor&quot;);
  aceeditor.setTheme(&quot;ace/theme/twilight&quot;);
  aceeditor.getSession().setMode(&quot;ace/mode/javascript&quot;);

  $(&quot;div&quot;).on(&#39;mouseenter&#39;,function(e) {
    var texteditor = $(&#39;textarea[id=&quot;texteditor&quot;]&#39;).hide();
    aceeditor.getSession().setValue(texteditor.val());
    aceeditor.getSession().on(&#39;change&#39;,function(e) {
      texteditor.val(aceeditor.getSession().getValue());
      texteditor.change();
    });
    
  });
&lt;/script&gt;</span><br></div><div>==========================</div><div>this is quite ugly, because the textarea is initally visible (and also the  $(&quot;div&quot;).on(&#39;mouseenter&#39;,function(e) {} seems like a hammer), but it is a little bit better...</div><div><br></div><div>If you have any idea on how to use livequery, I am interested.</div>
